// Design 177 in the profile it was asked for: a freestanding `-> Never` entry
// whose body IS the diverging loop. `-> Never` lowers to a `void` + `noreturn`
// C symbol (design 58), the loop needs no `break` to satisfy it, and the
// diverging loop's exit block is terminated with `unreachable` — so `kmain`
// emits as a bare back-edge and nothing else. This is the kernel halt shape.
//
// The `print` before it keeps the object honest about the profile: the write
// seam is left an UNDEFINED external for the environment to supply, and no
// runtime is linked beside it.
//
// (An ELF triple: the freestanding profile places per-symbol `.text.<name>`
// sections for `--gc-sections`, which the mach-O host rejects.)
// COMPILE-FLAGS: --freestanding --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
// EXPECT: object
// EXPECT-SYMBOL-UNDEFINED: __saw_rt_write

@export("kmain")
func kmain() -> Never {
    print("halting")
    while { }
}
